Article 3 (Requirements for Designation) (1) A local government may, by ordinance, designate a day as a local public holiday if all of the following requirements are met:
1. It is a commemorative day under the Regulations on Various Commemorative Days, etc.;
2. It is a day intended especially to commemorate a historical event that occurred in the relevant local government area;
3. It is a day capable of promoting unity and harmony among the residents of the relevant local government.
(2) If a local government intends to designate a local public holiday under paragraph (1), the head of that local government shall consult in advance with the head of the ministry or agency responsible for the relevant commemorative day pursuant to Article 2 (1) of the Regulations on Various Commemorative Days, etc.
